$$
 \lim_{x\to\infty}\\left(\frac{3+x}{6+x}\\right)^{\frac{x-1}{2}} 
$$
$$
 = \exp\left\{ \lim_{x\to\infty} \\left( \frac{3+x}{6+x} - 1 \\right) \cdot \frac{x-1}{2} \right\} 
$$
$$
 = \exp\left\{ \lim_{x\to\infty} \frac{-3}{x+6} \cdot \frac{x-1}{2} \right\} 
$$
